gpu-bridge: rebuild at the one pfifo-drain chokepoint, not per GL call

The renderer rebuilt gone-context GL objects only at the doors 0011/0012 named
one at a time - draw_begin, get_framebuffer_surface, sync, surface_update - so a
game that reached a gone object by some other method (a texture upload, a clear,
an image_blit) still aborted after a fresh-process savestate load. Move the
check to the single point that dominates every GL-touching path: the renderer's
process_pending op. pgraph_process_pending() calls it at the head of every pfifo
drain (pfifo_drain / pfifo_thread), before pfifo_run_pusher runs one pgraph
method and before the display path's pfifo_service_pending - so the first GL
touch of any kind after a load rebuilds first, at a shallow call depth, and no
later path can bind a gone name. Unconditional (a fresh load's first drain may
carry no pending flag) and a no-op once the objects match this session, so the
now-redundant per-door checks stay only as harmless belt-and-braces, and native
builds (context id 0) are unaffected. Read gl_renderer_state after the check:
a rebuild frees and reallocates it.

diff --git a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.c b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.c
--- a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.c
+++ b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.c
@@ -172,6 +172,27 @@
 static void pgraph_gl_process_pending(NV2AState *d)
 {
     PGRAPHState *pg = &d->pgraph;
+
+    /* THE cross-session rebuild point. pgraph_process_pending() calls this op
+     * at the head of every pfifo drain (pfifo_drain / pfifo_thread), before
+     * pfifo_run_pusher executes a single pgraph method and before the display
+     * path's pfifo_service_pending - so it runs ahead of EVERY GL-touching path
+     * there is: draw, clear_surface, image_blit, a texture or surface upload, a
+     * report. After a fresh-process savestate load the objects those paths
+     * reach name a host GL context that is gone; checking here rebuilds them
+     * once, up front and at a shallow call depth, so no later path can bind a
+     * gone name. Unconditional on purpose - not gated on a pending flag, since
+     * the drain that first touches GL after a load may carry none - and it is a
+     * no-op once the objects match this session (one bridge call, an integer
+     * compare), and entirely a no-op in the native reference build where the
+     * context id is 0. This is the one hook; the checks patch 0011/0012 put at
+     * draw_begin, get_framebuffer_surface, sync and surface_update are now
+     * redundant belt-and-braces (each a no-op once this has run). */
+    pgraph_gl_check_context(d);
+
+    /* read r only AFTER the check: a rebuild frees and reallocates
+     * gl_renderer_state (pgraph_gl_finalize/pgraph_gl_init), so a pointer taken
+     * before it would dangle. */
     PGRAPHGLState *r = pg->gl_renderer_state;
 
